IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `jcxv-core`

-- Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Qld) -- the seat of the party to a civil proceeding.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who brings or answers a civil claim (a plaintiff, a defendant, or a person who intervenes)
-- whose proceeding touches Queensland and another Australian jurisdiction: "Can my claim be heard in this court? Will
-- it be moved, and where to? Can I ask for it to be moved? Can my lawyer follow it? Which law decides it? Do the steps
-- already taken count? Where does my appeal go? Can I appeal the transfer? Can I enforce the judgment?" Every question
-- is asked as the party would ask it, on facts the party can state. A court's opinion or satisfaction is a fact the
-- party answers from what the court has said or found; it is never decided here. The rules are in jcxv-core.l4; this
-- module builds their inputs from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the same meaning have the same name
-- in every question.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Qld) -- the party's questions`

§§ `Does the Act reach my proceeding (ss 3, 3A, 4)`

@export Does the Queensland cross-vesting Act (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987) apply to my court proceeding at all? It does not apply to criminal proceedings or to the Corporations Act part 9.6A division 1 jurisdiction.
GIVEN `my proceeding is criminal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is a criminal prosecution or other criminal proceeding (answer no for a civil claim)
      `my proceeding is under Corporations Act part 9.6A division 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the jurisdiction in question is the corporations jurisdiction that the Corporations Act 2001 (Cth) part 9.6A division 1 deals with
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the cross-vesting Act apply to my proceeding` IS
    `the Act can apply to the proceeding (ss 3, 3A)` `my proceeding is criminal` `my proceeding is under Corporations Act part 9.6A division 1`

@export Is my claim a "State matter" under the Queensland cross-vesting Act: one the Supreme Court of Queensland could hear under Queensland law, or one removed to it under section 8?
GIVEN `the Supreme Court of Queensland could hear my claim under Queensland law alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court of Queensland has jurisdiction over your claim otherwise than because of a Commonwealth law or another State's law (for most claims under Queensland law or the common law in Queensland, yes)
      `my proceeding was removed to the Supreme Court under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court of Queensland has ordered your proceeding removed to it from a lower Queensland court or a tribunal under section 8
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim a State matter` IS
    `is a State matter (s 3(1))` `the Supreme Court of Queensland could hear my claim under Queensland law alone` `my proceeding was removed to the Supreme Court under section 8`

@export Can the Supreme Court (or State Family Court) of another State or Territory hear my Queensland claim, under the cross-vesting Act (s 4)?
GIVEN `the court I want to hear it` IS A `Court` @desc The court you want to hear your claim. One of: the Supreme Court of Queensland; the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory (including the NT and the ACT); the State Family Court of another State; the Federal Court; the Family Court; a court of Queensland other than the Supreme Court; a tribunal established by or under an Act; some other court
      `the Supreme Court of Queensland could hear my claim under Queensland law alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court of Queensland has jurisdiction over your claim otherwise than because of a Commonwealth law or another State's law
      `my proceeding was removed to the Supreme Court under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court of Queensland has ordered your proceeding removed to it from a lower Queensland court or a tribunal under section 8
      `my matter is criminal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter is a criminal matter
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can another State's Supreme Court hear my Queensland claim` IS
    `the court has jurisdiction in the State matter under s 4` `the court I want to hear it` (`is a State matter (s 3(1))` `the Supreme Court of Queensland could hear my claim under Queensland law alone` `my proceeding was removed to the Supreme Court under section 8`) `my matter is criminal`

@export Once my proceeding has been transferred to the Supreme Court of Queensland under a cross-vesting law, can that court hear and decide it (s 9)?
GIVEN `my proceeding was transferred to the Supreme Court of Queensland under a cross-vesting law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding was transferred to the Supreme Court of Queensland under this Act or under the Commonwealth's or another State's cross-vesting Act
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Supreme Court of Queensland hear my transferred proceeding` IS
    `the Supreme Court may hear the transferred proceeding (s 9)` `my proceeding was transferred to the Supreme Court of Queensland under a cross-vesting law`

§§ `Will my proceeding be moved to another court (ss 5, 6A)`

@export Must my proceeding be transferred from the court it is in to another court under section 5 of the Queensland cross-vesting Act, or may it be?
GIVEN `the court my proceeding is in` IS A `Court` @desc The court where your proceeding is now pending. One of: the Supreme Court of Queensland; the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory; the Federal Court; the Family Court; or another court listed
      `the court it would go to` IS A `Court` @desc The court it might be transferred to
      `a related proceeding of mine is pending in that other court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another proceeding that your proceeding arises out of, or is related to, is pending in the court it would go to
      `the court has found the other court more appropriate because of the related proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court your proceeding is in has found that, because of that related proceeding, it is more appropriate for the other court to decide yours
      `the court has found the other court more appropriate on the section 5 factors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court your proceeding is in has found it more appropriate for the other court to decide yours, having regard to where the proceeding could have been started without cross-vesting, how far it turns on the other jurisdiction's law, and the interests of justice
      `the court has found it otherwise in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court your proceeding is in has found that it is otherwise in the interests of justice for the other court to decide it (this ground does not apply to a move from the Supreme Court of Queensland to the Federal Court or Family Court)
      `section 6A applies to my proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether section 6A applies: a special federal matter under paragraph (c) or (e) about a Commonwealth authority or officer acting under a State enactment, related to a State matter proceeding pending in a Queensland court (ask the section 6A question if unsure)
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
DECIDE `Must my proceeding be transferred under section 5` IS
    `the s 5 transfer answer` (`Transfer facts` WITH
        `the first court` IS `the court my proceeding is in`
        `the other court` IS `the court it would go to`
        `a related proceeding is pending in the other court` IS `a related proceeding of mine is pending in that other court`
        `the first court finds the other court more appropriate because of the related proceeding` IS `the court has found the other court more appropriate because of the related proceeding`
        `the first court finds the other court more appropriate having regard to the s 5 factors` IS `the court has found the other court more appropriate on the section 5 factors`
        `the first court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice` IS `the court has found it otherwise in the interests of justice`
        `section 6A applies to the proceeding` IS `section 6A applies to my proceeding`)

@export One of my proceedings has been transferred to another court under a cross-vesting law. Must my other, related proceeding in the same court follow it (s 5(6))?
GIVEN `the court transferred one of my proceedings under a cross-vesting law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has transferred a proceeding to another court under this Act or another cross-vesting Act
      `another related proceeding of mine is still in that court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another proceeding that arises out of, or is related to, the transferred one is still pending in the court that transferred it
      `the court has found it in the interests of justice for the other court to decide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has found it in the interests of justice that the other court decide the related proceeding too
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my related proceeding follow the transferred one` IS
    `the related proceeding must follow (s 5(6))` `the court transferred one of my proceedings under a cross-vesting law` `another related proceeding of mine is still in that court` `the court has found it in the interests of justice for the other court to decide it`

@export Can I apply to the court to have my proceeding transferred under section 5 of the Queensland cross-vesting Act?
GIVEN `my role` IS A `Role in the proceeding` @desc Your role in the proceeding. One of: a party (plaintiff, applicant, defendant, respondent); a person who intervenes; someone else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply for a transfer` IS
    `may apply for a transfer (s 5(7))` `my role`

@export My proceeding has been transferred to another court under a cross-vesting law. Can my barrister or solicitor keep acting for me in the new court (s 5(8))?
GIVEN `my lawyer may practise in the court it came from` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your barrister or solicitor is entitled to practise in the court your proceeding was transferred from
      `my proceeding was transferred under a cross-vesting law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceeding was transferred to the other court under this Act or another cross-vesting Act
      `the question is about the transferred proceeding itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are asking about the transferred proceeding itself
      `the question is about a related proceeding to be decided together with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are asking about a related proceeding that the new court is to decide together with the transferred one
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my lawyer act for me in the new court` IS
    `the lawyer may practise in the other court (s 5(8))` `my lawyer may practise in the court it came from` `my proceeding was transferred under a cross-vesting law` `the question is about the transferred proceeding itself` `the question is about a related proceeding to be decided together with it`

§§ `Special federal matters (ss 6, 6A) -- only if your proceeding raises a special federal matter`

@export Does section 6A of the Queensland cross-vesting Act apply to my proceeding (a special federal matter about a Commonwealth authority or officer acting under a State law, related to a proceeding in a Queensland court)?
GIVEN `the special federal matter in my proceeding` IS A `Special federal matter` @desc Which paragraph of the definition of "special federal matter" in s 3(1) of the Commonwealth Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 your matter falls under. One of: none; paragraph (a), (b) or (d); paragraph (c) or (e); paragraph (ab)
      `it concerns a Commonwealth authority or officer acting under a State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter involves the exercise of functions or powers given to a Commonwealth authority or officer by a State enactment referred to in paragraph (ca) or (cb) of the definition of "enactment" in the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 (Cth)
      `a related State proceeding of mine is pending in a Queensland court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter arises out of, or relates to, another proceeding pending in any Queensland court (whichever was started first)
      `that State proceeding arises mainly under that State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that other proceeding arises, wholly or substantially, under that State enactment or a corresponding enactment of another State
      `that State proceeding has no paragraph (c) or (e) matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether none of the matters in that other proceeding is a special federal matter under paragraph (c) or (e)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 6A apply to my proceeding` IS
    `section 6A applies (s 6A(1))` `the special federal matter in my proceeding` `it concerns a Commonwealth authority or officer acting under a State law` `a related State proceeding of mine is pending in a Queensland court` `that State proceeding arises mainly under that State law` `that State proceeding has no paragraph (c) or (e) matter`

@export My proceeding in the Supreme Court of Queensland raises a special federal matter. Must it go to the Federal Court or the Family Court, and which (s 6)?
GIVEN `my proceeding is in the Supreme Court of Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is pending in the Supreme Court of Queensland
      `the special federal matter in my proceeding` IS A `Special federal matter` @desc Which paragraph of the definition of "special federal matter" in s 3(1) of the Commonwealth Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 your matter falls under. One of: none; paragraph (a), (b) or (d); paragraph (c) or (e); paragraph (ab)
      `the Supreme Court has ordered that it will decide my proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has made an order under s 6(3) that it will determine the proceeding itself
      `section 6A applies to my proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether section 6A applies (ask the section 6A question if unsure)
      `mine is an appeal to the Full Court where the court below ordered under s 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is an appeal to the Full Court (Court of Appeal) of the Supreme Court from a decision of a court that had made an s 6(3) order about the special federal matter
GIVETH A `Special federal matter answer`
DECIDE `Must my special federal matter go to a federal court` IS
    `the s 6 answer` `my proceeding is in the Supreme Court of Queensland` `the special federal matter in my proceeding` `the Supreme Court has ordered that it will decide my proceeding` `section 6A applies to my proceeding` `mine is an appeal to the Full Court where the court below ordered under s 6(3)`

@export Can the Supreme Court of Queensland keep my proceeding although it raises a special federal matter (s 6(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied there are special reasons, not just convenience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has said it is satisfied that there are special reasons, in the particular circumstances, for it to decide the proceeding, other than reasons about the parties' convenience
      `written notice went to both Attorneys-General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a written notice stating the nature of the special federal matter has been given to the Commonwealth Attorney-General and the Queensland Attorney-General
      `the court is satisfied a reasonable time has passed since the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court is satisfied that a reasonable time has passed since the notice for the Attorneys-General to consider making submissions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` IS
    `the Supreme Court may order that it determine the proceeding (s 6(3), (4))` `the court is satisfied there are special reasons, not just convenience` `written notice went to both Attorneys-General` `the court is satisfied a reasonable time has passed since the notice`

@export The Supreme Court of Queensland directed me to give the Attorneys-General written notice of the special federal matter in my case. By when must I give it (s 6(5)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the court directed me` IS A DATE @desc The day the Supreme Court directed you to give the notice
      `the days the court allowed me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the court's direction allows for giving the notice (the Act fixes none; the court's direction does)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give the special federal matter notice` IS
    `the day` `the days the court allowed me` `days after` `the day the court directed me`

@export Did I give the Attorneys-General the notice of the special federal matter that the Supreme Court directed, in time (s 6(5)(b))? Yes, no, or not yet known while time is still running.
GIVEN `the day the court directed me` IS A DATE @desc The day the Supreme Court directed you to give the notice
      `the days the court allowed me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the court's direction allows for giving the notice
      `I have given the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given written notice of the special federal matter to both the Commonwealth and the Queensland Attorneys-General
      `the day I gave the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the notice to the second of the two Attorneys-General (any day if not yet given)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I give the special federal matter notice in time` IS
    IF `I have given the notice`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 6(5)(b) -- the notice the court directed a party to give` `the days the court allowed me`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the directed party` `give written notice of the special federal matter to both Attorneys-General` (`the days from` `the day the court directed me` `to` `the day I gave the notice`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (`the days from` `the day the court directed me` `to` `today`) GREATER THAN `the days the court allowed me`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING

@export My proceeding raises a special federal matter. Does section 6 stop the Supreme Court of Queensland giving me urgent interim relief (s 6(7))?
GIVEN `the court finds urgent interim relief in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has found it in the interests of justice to grant urgent relief of an interlocutory (interim) nature
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Supreme Court give me urgent interim relief despite the special federal matter` IS
    `s 6 does not stop urgent interlocutory relief (s 6(7))` `the court finds urgent interim relief in the interests of justice`

@export The Supreme Court of Queensland decided my case although it raised a special federal matter, without an s 6(3) order or the notice to the Attorneys-General. Does section 6 make its decision invalid (s 6(8))?
GIVEN `the Supreme Court decided my special federal matter without the order or notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court determined your proceeding, which raised a special federal matter, without an s 6(3) order or without the notice to the Attorneys-General being given
      `it did so by inadvertence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that happened through inadvertence (oversight)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 6 invalidate the decision in my case` IS
    `s 6 invalidates the decision` `the Supreme Court decided my special federal matter without the order or notice` `it did so by inadvertence`

§§ `Appeals (s 7) -- only if you want to appeal`

@export Can I appeal from the Federal Court or the Family Court to the Court of Appeal (Full Court of the Supreme Court of Queensland), or from one of those federal courts to the other (s 7(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the decision I want to appeal from` IS A `Decision appealed from` @desc Whose decision you want to appeal. One of: a single Judge of the Federal Court; a single Judge of the Family Court; the Full Court of the Federal Court; the Full Court of the Family Court
      `the court I want to appeal to` IS AN `Appeal court` @desc The court you want to appeal to. One of: the Full Court of the Supreme Court of Queensland (the Court of Appeal); the Federal Court; the Family Court; the High Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I appeal from the federal court to that court` IS
    `an appeal may be instituted from the federal court (s 7(1), (2))` `the decision I want to appeal from` `the court I want to appeal to`

@export I want to appeal from a single Judge of the Supreme Court of Queensland in a case that was cross-vested. Which court must my appeal go to (s 7(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `a matter in my appeal arises under an Act in the Commonwealth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any matter for determination in your appeal arises under an Act listed in the Schedule to the Commonwealth Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Commonwealth Acts usually heard in the Federal Court or Family Court)
      `the decision was a State Family Court Judge's and my appeal also involves another matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was given by a Judge of a State Family Court and your appeal involves both a Schedule-Act matter and another matter
GIVETH AN `Appeal route answer`
DECIDE `Where must my appeal go` IS
    `the s 7 appeal route` `a matter in my appeal arises under an Act in the Commonwealth Schedule` `the decision was a State Family Court Judge's and my appeal also involves another matter`

@export The Court of Appeal (Full Court of the Supreme Court of Queensland) has begun hearing my appeal, and it now appears to raise a Schedule-Act matter. Must it transfer my appeal to the Full Court of the Federal Court or Family Court (s 7(6))?
GIVEN `the Full Court has begun hearing my appeal and not yet decided it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Full Court has begun to hear your appeal and has not yet determined it
      `it appears to the Full Court that my appeal is an s 7(4) appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Full Court that a matter in your appeal arises under an Act in the Schedule to the Commonwealth cross-vesting Act (and s 7(5) does not apply)
      `the Full Court finds the interests of justice require it to go on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Full Court has found that the interests of justice require it to go on and decide the appeal itself
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my appeal be transferred to the federal Full Court` IS
    `the Full Court must transfer the appeal (s 7(6))` `the Full Court has begun hearing my appeal and not yet decided it` `it appears to the Full Court that my appeal is an s 7(4) appeal` `the Full Court finds the interests of justice require it to go on`

@export The Court of Appeal (Full Court of the Supreme Court of Queensland) decided my appeal although it raised a Schedule-Act matter. Does section 7 make the decision invalid (s 7(7))?
GIVEN `the Full Court decided my s 7(4) appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Full Court determined your appeal although a matter in it arose under an Act in the Schedule to the Commonwealth cross-vesting Act
      `it went on because the interests of justice required it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it went on to decide because it found the interests of justice required it (s 7(6))
      `it did so by inadvertence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it did so through inadvertence (oversight)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 7 invalidate the decision on my appeal` IS
    `s 7 invalidates the decision` `the Full Court decided my s 7(4) appeal` `it went on because the interests of justice required it` `it did so by inadvertence`

§§ `Removal from a lower court or tribunal; consumer law transfers (ss 8, 10)`

@export My proceeding is in a lower Queensland court or a tribunal. Can the Supreme Court of Queensland remove it to itself (s 8(1))? A party may apply, or the court may act of its own motion.
GIVEN `the court my proceeding is in` IS A `Court` @desc The court or tribunal where your proceeding is pending. One of: a court of Queensland other than the Supreme Court; a tribunal established by or under an Act; or another court listed
      `a related proceeding of mine is in the Federal Court, the Family Court or another Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding arises out of, or is related to, another proceeding pending in the Federal Court, the Family Court or the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory
      `the Supreme Court finds that other proceeding could then be transferred to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has found that, if it removed your proceeding, there would be grounds to transfer that other proceeding to it
      `the Supreme Court finds removal needed to consider a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has found that it should remove your proceeding so that it can consider whether to transfer it to another court
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Supreme Court remove my proceeding to itself` IS
    `the Supreme Court may remove the proceeding (s 8(1))` `the court my proceeding is in` `a related proceeding of mine is in the Federal Court, the Family Court or another Supreme Court` `the Supreme Court finds that other proceeding could then be transferred to it` `the Supreme Court finds removal needed to consider a transfer`

@export My proceeding was removed to the Supreme Court of Queensland under section 8. Can it be sent back to the court or tribunal it came from (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `my proceeding was removed under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court ordered your proceeding removed to it under s 8(1)
      `the Supreme Court considers sending it back appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has said it considers it appropriate to send the proceeding back
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my removed proceeding be sent back` IS
    `the Supreme Court may remit the proceeding (s 8(3))` `my proceeding was removed under section 8` `the Supreme Court considers sending it back appropriate`

@export My Australian Consumer Law claim is in a Supreme Court. Can it be transferred down to a lower Queensland court (s 10)? A party may apply, or the court may act of its own motion.
GIVEN `the court my proceeding is in` IS A `Court` @desc The court where your proceeding is pending. One of: the Supreme Court of Queensland; the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory; or another court listed
      `my claim arises under the listed consumer law provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a matter in your claim arises under the Australian Consumer Law (Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth) schedule 2, applying as a Commonwealth law) chapter 3 part 3-1 divisions 1, 2, 4 or 5 (unsolicited supplies, lay-by and similar), part 3-3 (safety of consumer goods) or part 3-4 (information standards)
      `no matter in my proceeding is a special federal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether none of the matters in your proceeding is a special federal matter
      `my proceeding is an appeal from a court's judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is an appeal from a judgment of a court
      `a lower Queensland court could hear every matter in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Queensland court other than the Supreme Court (for example the District or Magistrates Court) has jurisdiction over all the matters in your proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my consumer law proceeding be transferred to a lower Queensland court` IS
    `the court may transfer the consumer law proceeding to a lower Queensland court (s 10)` `the court my proceeding is in` `my claim arises under the listed consumer law provisions` `no matter in my proceeding is a special federal matter` `my proceeding is an appeal from a court's judgment` `a lower Queensland court could hear every matter in it`

§§ `After a transfer: law, steps, costs, appeal, enforcement (ss 11-14)`

@export The court hearing my claim is exercising cross-vested jurisdiction. Which State's or Territory's law will it apply to my claim (s 11(1))? (Rules of evidence and procedure are as the court considers appropriate.)
GIVEN `the court is likely to exercise cross-vested jurisdiction in my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the court that it will, or is likely to, exercise jurisdiction given by this Act or another cross-vesting Act in deciding your claim
      `my right of action arises under a written law of another State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your right of action arises under a statute (written law) of a State or Territory other than the one where the court is sitting
GIVETH AN `Applicable law answer`
DECIDE `Which law will the court apply to my claim` IS
    `the s 11 applicable law` `the court is likely to exercise cross-vested jurisdiction in my claim` `my right of action arises under a written law of another State or Territory`

@export My proceeding was transferred or removed to another court. Do the steps already taken in the first court (including its orders) count in the new court (s 11(3))?
GIVEN `my proceeding was transferred or removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding was transferred or removed to another court
      `the new court has ordered otherwise about that step` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new court has made an order that the step, or that kind of step, is not to be treated as taken before it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the steps already taken count in the new court` IS
    `the earlier step counts in the transferee court (s 11(3))` `my proceeding was transferred or removed` `the new court has ordered otherwise about that step`

@export My proceeding was transferred or removed. Can the new court make an order about the costs of the proceeding before the transfer (s 12)?
GIVEN `my proceeding was transferred or removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding was transferred or removed to another court
      `another court has already dealt with those costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs of the proceeding before the transfer or removal have already been dealt with by another court
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the new court order costs for the earlier part` IS
    `the new court may order the earlier costs (s 12)` `my proceeding was transferred or removed` `another court has already dealt with those costs`

@export Can I appeal against the court's decision to transfer or remove my proceeding, or its decision about which rules of evidence and procedure apply (s 13)?
GIVEN `the decision I want to appeal` IS A `Decision kind` @desc The decision you want to appeal. One of: a decision about transferring or removing the proceeding under this Act; a decision about which rules of evidence and procedure apply under s 11(1); some other decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I appeal that decision` IS
    `an appeal lies from the decision (s 13)` `the decision I want to appeal`

@export I have a judgment of the Supreme Court of Queensland given in cross-vested jurisdiction. Can I enforce it in Queensland like any other Supreme Court judgment (s 14(1))?
GIVEN `my judgment is a Supreme Court of Queensland judgment given at least partly in cross-vested jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your judgment was given by the Supreme Court of Queensland, wholly or partly in the exercise of jurisdiction given by a cross-vesting law
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I enforce my cross-vested judgment in Queensland` IS
    `the judgment is enforceable as an ordinary Supreme Court judgment (s 14(1))` `my judgment is a Supreme Court of Queensland judgment given at least partly in cross-vested jurisdiction`
